Dear Ms. Rinfret,

Thank you for your email of April 16, 2026 regarding File A-2026-00130 (TBS portal: EA2026_0167940).

Please direct all future correspondence for this file to: [redacted]

OPIs: Yes, this request is seeking records from RCN, CJOC, JAG, and VCDS as specified in the original. I am not able to limit the initial search to RCN only. The four named OPIs hold different, non-overlapping record types: posting orders and operational assignment records (CJOC / Naval Personnel and Training Group), legal opinions on personnel placement in foreign military law jurisdictions (JAG), personnel policy guidance (VCDS), and naval administrative records (RCN). A search limited to RCN would be structurally incomplete — the most sensitive records relevant to this request are unlikely to reside in RCN administrative files alone.

Timeframe: I am maintaining the original timeframe of January 1, 2024 to April 11, 2026 (inclusive). The bilateral defence framework was negotiated through 2024, and operational planning for an embedded exchange aboard a foreign naval vessel is a multi-month process. Selection criteria for the embedded positions would have been developed well before the vessel's March 2026 departure. Restricting to January 1, 2026 — a 90-day window — would exclude all pre-deployment planning, criteria development, and any legal or duty-of-care assessments conducted during the planning phase.

Record versions: I do not consent to a limitation to final versions only. Please include all responsive records regardless of draft status — including posting discussion email chains, working drafts of selection criteria, and intermediate assessments — subject to applicable exemptions and severance under s. 25.

Keywords: I confirm that the keywords are used in the context of RCN personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho, consistent with your suggestion.

Rescope structure: Your rescope items 1 through 4 are acceptable as a structural framework, subject to the timeframe, OPI, and draft-version corrections above, with the following required addition as a distinct fifth search category:

Records indicating whether the sexual orientation, gender, or gender identity of candidates was considered — directly or indirectly — in the selection process for the embedded positions, including any records reflecting guidance provided to selecting officials regarding Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea's Military Criminal Act; and any records indicating whether disclosure was provided to, or withheld from, selected personnel regarding the legal environment applicable to Article 92-6 aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho.

This item addresses whether DND's duty of care obligations were met at the individual personnel level. It is legally distinct from whether a policy analysis was conducted and is not captured by any of the four items in your rescope suggestion. It corresponds directly to items 3 and 4 of the original request description.

Please proceed with processing on this basis.

Thank you for your assistance.

Gender Watchdog
