Good day,

As per our phone call, and further to your currently ON HOLD Access to Information request:

Records requested: All records held by the Department of National Defence concerning the selection, posting, and assignment of Royal Canadian Navy (RCN) personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho (Republic of Korea Navy, KSS-III class submarine) during its trans-Pacific voyage to Canada in 2026, specifically:

All records concerning the criteria used to select RCN personnel for the embedded exchange positions aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho, including posting instructions, selection criteria, eligibility requirements, or any restrictions or considerations applied to the selection process;

Any assessments, communications, or briefings concerning the legal, human rights, or personnel policy implications of placing CAF members aboard a vessel governed by Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea's Military Criminal Act, which criminalizes consensual same-sex conduct between military personnel;

Any records indicating whether the sexual orientation, gender, or gender identity of candidates was considered — directly or indirectly — in the selection process for the embedded positions, including any records reflecting guidance to selecting officials regarding the Korean Military Criminal Act;

Any duty of care assessments, risk assessments, or briefings concerning the legal environment applicable to RCN personnel serving aboard a Korean naval vessel — including any disclosure provided to or withheld from selected personnel regarding Article 92-6;

Any communications between DND, CJOC, NDHQ, or the Naval Personnel and Training Group concerning the embedded posting, including the timeline and authority for the assignment decision.

Record types: Posting orders, assignment instructions, selection criteria documents, emails, briefing notes, legal opinions, duty of care assessments, memos, GCdocs/InfoBank entries, Teams chats, HRMS entries.

Search locations/systems: Canadian Joint Operations Command (CJOC); Naval Personnel and Training Group (NPTG); NDHQ personnel assignment desks; Judge Advocate General (JAG); VCDS personnel policy branch.

Keywords: "Dosan Ahn Chang-ho"; "KSS-III"; "embedded"; "exchange personnel"; "posting criteria"; "selection criteria"; "Article 92-6"; "Korean Military Criminal Act"; "sexual orientation"; "LGBTQ"; "homosexual"; "duty of care"; "personnel exchange Korea"; "joint exercises Korea"; "trans-Pacific"; "Esquimalt exchange".

Note: Interpret keywords broadly per s.4(2.1). Records may be indexed using operational language — terms such as "Korea exchange," "submarine exchange posting," "KSS-III liaison," or "Esquimalt Korea personnel" should be included. A nil result should be reported as such rather than a non-response.

Severance/duty to assist: Please sever and release all non-exempt information (s.25) and apply the duty to assist (s.4(2.1)). Rolling/interim releases preferred. Delivery preference: electronic.

In order to proceed with the processing of your request, we require the following clarification of your phrasing and the target of this request.

Is this request seeking records from RCN, CJOC, JAG and VCDS?
I might suggest it would be helpful to start with only RCN and request their input on further areas to target.

Please note that your request is very broad in scope and may generate a large volume of documents which may take months/significant time to process/significantly delay the response. In order to ensure you receive the relevant information you’re seeking in a timely fashion, it may be advantageous to you to narrow the scope of your search. In a case such as yours we often suggest asking for only certain documents (emails or briefing notes for example), targeting a more specific subject, or narrowing down the time frame. The choice to re-scope your initial request is made completely at your discretion.

Regarding the keywords provided, please confirm whether they are related to the RCN personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho. Searching these keywords on their own will generate a large volume of records, many of which would not be relevant to the purpose of this request.

Suggested rescope:

Final versions of records (briefing notes, memos, legal opinions, risk assessments, posting orders, assignment instructions, selection criteria documents, and email correspondence) held by RCN related to the selection, posting, and assignment of Royal Canadian Navy personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho (Republic of Korea Navy, KSS-III class submarine) during its trans-Pacific voyage from January 1 2026 – April 11, 2026, including:

  Records describing the selection process, criteria, eligibility requirements, and authority for assigning RCN personnel to embedded positions aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho (Republic of Korea Navy, KSS-III class submarine)

  Records related to the deployment of CAF members aboard a Republic of Korea Navy vessel, including consideration of applicable Korean military law (including Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea’s Military Criminal Act)

  Records concerning the legal, human rights, or personnel policy implications of placing CAF members aboard a vessel governed by Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea's Military Criminal Act, which criminalizes consensual same-sex conduct between military personnel

  Records concerning the embedded posting, including the timeline and authority for the assignment decision.

Please use these keywords only in the context of RCN personnel embedded aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho, and not as standalone search terms: "Dosan Ahn Chang-ho"; "KSS-III"; "embedded"; "exchange personnel"; "posting criteria"; "selection criteria"; "Article 92-6"; "Korean Military Criminal Act"; "sexual orientation"; "LGBTQ"; "homosexual"; "duty of care"; "personnel exchange Korea"; "joint exercises Korea"; "trans-Pacific"; "Esquimalt exchange".

Note, if you accept this rescope suggestion, our subject matter experts may have further rescope suggestions, or clarification questions.

Please advise if this reflects the intent of your request, if you have any additional suggestions, amendments and how you wish to proceed.

If you agree, we require your consent to change the wording of your request in writing, as per section 6 of the Access to Information Act, your response via email will suffice.

Please let me know if I can be of further assistance in this matter.

Thank you,

